      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T22:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The hash.h and hash.c edit history is a bit convoluted, but it went out like this:\n\n1. Initial files were added with CL 20160 (for `hash_me`), with the custom CRC24 implementation.\n2. Hashing for intrabc was implemented with CL 23580, which leveraged the existing CRC24 implementation.\n3. A SSE4 CRC32C routine was added to accelerate `hash_me` (but not intrabc)\n4. A C-only CRC32C routine was added to avoid SIMD/C output mismatch, and `hash_me` was modified to use CRC32C (but not intrabc)\n5. CL 201221 (this change) swaps CRC24 intrabc with CRC32C to align with `hash_me`, and deletes the original CRC24 implementation\n\nThis has two consequences:\n1. With this CL, the code in hash.h and hash.c is only used by CRC32C, so there\u0027s no need to move it to a separate file (maybe rename to crc32c.h and crc32c.c)\n2. `AOM_BUFFER_SIZE_FOR_BLOCK_HASH` is used for intrabc hashing, so we want to keep the `#define` around, maybe move it to some other header file (like `intra_mode_search_utils.h`)?",
      "parentUuid": "60e74c05_8695bafd",
      "revId": "d35d69a9d3073ea4fad44bd643bebec253f14470",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
